* [`ag.modcurve.xnsp`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Background/Algebraic-geometry/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_ag___modcurve___xnsp_FLQQ_--statement) — Modular curve \$X\_\{\\text\{ns\}\}\^\{+\}(N)\$. Kind: Errors in the text, Conflicting definitions, Suggested recategorisations. Category: Error or typo (for the editors to decide); Conflict; Suggested category: modcurve.

  For N with r distinct prime factors, a Cartan subgroup C of GL₂(ℤ/Nℤ) = ∏\_ℓ GL₂(ℤ/ℓ\^e) that is nonsplit at every ℓ \| N is ∏\_ℓ C\_ℓ, and its normalizer ∏\_ℓ N(C\_ℓ) contains C with index 2\^r, while the extended Cartan subgroup E (C and the canonical involution, gl2.cartan), which modcurve.xns\_plus uses for the same curve X\_ns⁺(N), contains C with index 2. By brute force \[N(C) : C\] = \[E : C\] = 2 for N = 2, 3, 4, 5, 7, 8, 9, but \[N(C) : C\] = 4 and \[E : C\] = 2 for N = 6, 10, 12, 14, 15, so the two knowls define different curves unless N is a prime power. Also, gl2.nonsplit\_cartan defines non-split Cartan subgroups of GL₂(𝔽\_p) only. The replacement follows modcurve.xns\_plus; if the database's X\_ns⁺(N) is the curve of the full normalizer, keep "normalizer" here, of a Cartan subgroup of GL₂(ℤ/Nℤ) that is nonsplit at every prime dividing N, and change modcurve.xns\_plus instead. — Conflicting definition: Conflicts with 'modcurve.xns\_plus': normaliser vs extended Cartan: different groups when N has two or more prime factors. — Suggested recategorisation: The modular curve X\_ns\^+(N); duplicates modcurve.xns\_plus.

