* [`shimcurve.nrdmu`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Varieties/Shimura-curves/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_shimcurve___nrdmu_FLQQ_--statement) — Polarization degree of a polarized order. Kind: Errors in the text. Category: Error or typo (for the editors to decide).

  With the polarizations of shimcurve.polarized\_order, nrd(μ)/discrd(O) need not be an integer: in B = (−1, 3 / ℚ), ramified exactly at 2 and 3, the order O = ℤ + ℤi + ℤj + ℤij has disc(O) = \|det diag(2, −2, 6, 6)\| = 144, so discrd(O) = 12, and μ = i is a polarization (μ² = −1 and iO ⊆ O) with nrd(μ)/discrd(O) = 1/12, or 1/6 in a maximal order containing O. Since nrd(μ) = −μ² is an integer, one fix is to take the square-free part of the integer nrd(μ)·discrd(O), which has the same square class as nrd(μ)/discrd(O); another is to strengthen the condition on μ so that discrd(O) divides nrd(μ). Which one matches the database's polarization degrees is for the editors to decide. Also: The replacement that the formalisation follows (PolarizedQuaternionOrder.polarizationDegree in LeanBridge): the polarization degree is the square-free part of the positive rational number nrd(mu)/discrd(O), which need not be an integer.

  Old:

